- Let’s see...

4
00:00:20,840 --> 00:00:22,800
- Give me your hand.
- There.

5
00:00:23,920 --> 00:00:27,040
- Is this pinned to the wall?
- Wait, I’ll lift it.

6
00:00:27,160 --> 00:00:28,720
One, two, three.

7
00:00:29,240 --> 00:00:33,160
Hold on, my hand, my hand.
Wait a minute.

8
00:00:34,360 --> 00:00:37,560
It’s falling apart. It definitely is!

9
00:00:37,720 --> 00:00:40,680
- Pull that edge. One, two, three.
- OK.

10
00:00:43,880 --> 00:00:44,880
That’s enough.

11
00:00:46,360 --> 00:00:47,240
Enough.

12
00:00:48,520 --> 00:00:50,280
You know the saying:

13
00:00:51,440 --> 00:00:56,800
- "When a door closes..."
- A window opens.

14
00:00:56,880 --> 00:00:58,280
That’s right.

15
00:00:58,520 --> 00:01:01,480
Now it starts
what I like to call The Hunt.

16
00:01:02,840 --> 00:01:05,640
- For talent.
- It’s implicit in The Hunt.

17
00:01:05,720 --> 00:01:08,240
- The Hunt.
- We won’t kill animals, Magüi.

18
00:01:08,400 --> 00:01:13,280
Well, we’re looking
for a triple threat actress.

19
00:01:13,520 --> 00:01:15,840
Good in drama and comedy,

20
00:01:15,960 --> 00:01:19,480
a good singer and dancer.
That’s a great bonus.

21
00:01:19,560 --> 00:01:23,120
- We like a good personality.
- Well, that’s important.

22
00:01:23,200 --> 00:01:24,680
- It’s not bad.
- That she is a...

23
00:01:24,760 --> 00:01:26,560
Being a good person
is desirable in life.

24
00:01:26,640 --> 00:01:27,960
That she’s supportive.

25
00:01:29,760 --> 00:01:31,400
It’s also important that she’s cute.

26
00:01:31,480 --> 00:01:35,200
- Don’t you think?
- If she’s cute, she’ll sell.

27
00:01:35,280 --> 00:01:38,120
Yeah, that’s good.
Well, a triple threat actress...

28
00:01:38,200 --> 00:01:39,600
For instance...

29
00:01:41,440 --> 00:01:42,920
For instance, Natalie Portman.

30
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:44,960
- Natalie Portman.
- She is the perfect example

31
00:01:45,040 --> 00:01:47,160
of a triple threat actress.
Anne Hathaway.

32
00:01:47,240 --> 00:01:50,320
- Anne Hathaway.
- Michelle Jenner. Toni Acosta.

33
00:01:53,520 --> 00:01:56,120
- Paquita is all right.
- I’d like to have breakfast.

34
00:01:56,200 --> 00:01:58,240
I’m having this because I woke up early.

35
00:02:00,040 --> 00:02:02,960
Breakfast is very important, it really is.

36
00:02:03,040 --> 00:02:04,880
It’s the most important meal of the day.

37
00:02:06,200 --> 00:02:08,160
Macarena never liked to have breakfast.

38
00:02:08,920 --> 00:02:11,320
She never had breakfast.
I always told her to.

39
00:02:11,400 --> 00:02:12,840
She was very thin.

40
00:02:14,120 --> 00:02:16,360
She had lunch, but never breakfast.

41
00:03:04,480 --> 00:03:06,600
Well, this is the videobooks shelf.

42
00:03:06,680 --> 00:03:10,680
So, each time PS Management
gets one by email

43
00:03:10,760 --> 00:03:12,120
or somebody dropped them...

44
00:03:12,200 --> 00:03:13,560
- By courier service.
- Exactly.

45
00:03:13,640 --> 00:03:18,520
We put them here and now it’s time
to watch them and see what we find out.

46
00:03:18,720 --> 00:03:19,520
Look.

47
00:03:19,960 --> 00:03:21,840
This boy is from “Física y Química”.

48
00:03:21,920 --> 00:03:24,320
- He was very good and very cute.
- Nobody calls him.

49
00:03:24,400 --> 00:03:25,720
- Nobody.
- You must be careful

50
00:03:25,800 --> 00:03:27,520
with gay roles. It’s true.

51
00:03:27,600 --> 00:03:29,920
- We love gays, but...
- Specially if you are gay.

52
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:33,680
It’s complicated,
sometimes you can be typecast.

53
00:03:33,760 --> 00:03:37,280
Then you have
to play that role. Evidently.

54
00:03:38,200 --> 00:03:41,120
- What a career, right?
- Look, Miguel Ángel Muñoz.

55
00:03:41,360 --> 00:03:44,640
He started with us. A triple threat.
People think there’s no talent

56
00:03:44,720 --> 00:03:47,600
in Spain. There’s a lot.
Don’t be fooled.

57
00:03:47,680 --> 00:03:51,760
A lot of people, great diversity.
Manoli, very intense. Pretty, right?

58
00:03:51,920 --> 00:03:54,680
It was a good picture choice
and she has a single name.

59
00:03:54,840 --> 00:03:56,720
The name is key.

60
00:03:56,800 --> 00:03:59,080
- You know who they are.
- That’s right, for instance...

61
00:03:59,600 --> 00:04:02,120
- Silke.
- Silke, great example.

62
00:04:02,360 --> 00:04:04,000
- Carmen.
- Carmen.

63
00:04:04,080 --> 00:04:05,320
Which Carmen?

64
00:04:05,720 --> 00:04:08,320
- Machi.
- No, Carmen Sevilla.

65
00:04:08,400 --> 00:04:10,320
You hear “Carmen”
and you know who that is.

66
00:04:10,400 --> 00:04:11,640
May she rest in peace.

67
00:04:11,720 --> 00:04:13,960
What’s this?
There are many things.

68
00:04:14,040 --> 00:04:15,920
Let’s see, what else have we got?

69
00:04:17,680 --> 00:04:19,600
- We’ve already seen these.
- This one neither.

70
00:04:20,920 --> 00:04:21,960
God!

71
00:04:22,040 --> 00:04:26,080
A black man. It’s always good
to have a black man in our portfolio.

72
00:04:26,160 --> 00:04:27,160
Yeah.

73
00:04:31,320 --> 00:04:35,560
-Aki... Aki Fandel.
-Akif Ndel.

74
00:04:35,720 --> 00:04:39,760
They’ve cast many black men
in “Mar de Plástico”.

75
00:04:39,840 --> 00:04:41,640
There are many black women
in “Vis a Vis”.

76
00:04:41,720 --> 00:04:44,600
And many gypsies.
It’s true that we have

77
00:04:44,800 --> 00:04:46,800
- to widen our horizons.
- It was about time.

78
00:04:46,880 --> 00:04:49,520
You’re right.
Put it aside, we’ll watch it.

79
00:04:49,600 --> 00:04:51,640
Perhaps he’s a diamond in the rough.

80
00:04:51,720 --> 00:04:54,560
Sometimes they cast a black man
for the role of the protagonist.

81
00:04:55,240 --> 00:04:56,760
- Good morning.
- Hi.

82
00:04:56,840 --> 00:04:58,560
I’ve got a delivery for Jorge Robelas.

83
00:04:58,640 --> 00:05:00,960
- Can I get a sign here?
- Magüi, I’ll turn this off.

84
00:05:01,040 --> 00:05:03,080
It’s unbearable!
He isn’t a triple threat!

85
00:05:03,160 --> 00:05:05,320
Is nobody talented?
What’s going on!

86
00:05:07,360 --> 00:05:08,360
Fuck off!

87
00:05:10,080 --> 00:05:12,080
- How is she?
- Better.

88
00:05:12,440 --> 00:05:14,960
I hid the chocolate rolls
from her, otherwise...

89
00:05:15,680 --> 00:05:18,120
- How are you?
- I’m fine.

90
00:05:19,200 --> 00:05:23,160
Listen, I left a joint here yesterday.
Have you seen it?

91
00:05:26,360 --> 00:05:29,760
- Leave it. Perhaps she’ll chill.
- No, this isn’t it! This isn’t it!

92
00:05:29,880 --> 00:05:32,400
Paquita, have you watched
my cousin’s videobook?

93
00:05:32,480 --> 00:05:34,400
- I sent it to you yesterday.
- Have I seen

94
00:05:34,480 --> 00:05:36,880
your cousin’s videobook?
What kind of question is that?

95
00:05:36,960 --> 00:05:39,720
But next week she’ll be
on the FHM magazine,

96
00:05:39,800 --> 00:05:41,880
- isn’t that important?
- Great, good for her.

97
00:05:41,960 --> 00:05:45,200
We check all the girls on that magazine.
All of them.

98
00:05:46,640 --> 00:05:47,520
All right.

99
00:05:48,160 --> 00:05:49,760
- Bye, handsome.
- Bye.

100
00:05:50,160 --> 00:05:54,200
This isn’t it! I’ve finished this pile!
Magüi, bring me more, please.

101
00:05:54,280 --> 00:05:57,160
No way, how is this possible!
We found her.

102
00:05:57,560 --> 00:05:59,480
I’ll call her
and give her the good news.

103
00:06:01,640 --> 00:06:04,960
- Hi. Hiba? Hiba Abouk?
<i>- Yeah, hello</i>?

104
00:06:05,040 --> 00:06:07,120
I’m calling from PS Management.
Paquita Salas.

105
00:06:07,200 --> 00:06:08,560
I have some news for you.
Are you seated?

106
00:06:08,640 --> 00:06:11,960
<i>- Yeah, I’m listening</i>.
- Look, we’ve seen your portfolio.

107
00:06:12,040 --> 00:06:14,160
We really liked it.
Tell me something, darling,

108
00:06:14,240 --> 00:06:18,560
- where are you from? Which hood?
<i>- Can you give me the address</i>?

109
00:06:19,080 --> 00:06:23,320
- It’s you, right? Your videobook...
<i>- Sure, it’s just that..</i>.

110
00:06:24,160 --> 00:06:27,600
She hung up on me.
She said she sent it years ago.

111
00:06:28,360 --> 00:06:31,640
I wanted to tell you
before calling her, but...

112
00:06:31,760 --> 00:06:34,560
She’s the protagonist of "El Príncipe".

113
00:06:35,440 --> 00:06:37,200
But that series
doesn’t have many viewers.

114
00:06:37,280 --> 00:06:40,240
Well, around six millions.
Five or six.

115
00:06:40,320 --> 00:06:42,760
Of people?
That’s like twenty...

116
00:06:42,840 --> 00:06:45,680
It’s twenty-five
or twenty-seven of share.

117
00:06:45,760 --> 00:06:47,880
Well, that’s a huge audience.
Is her role important?

118
00:06:47,960 --> 00:06:50,360
- Has she got many lines?
- And lot of nudes.

119
00:06:51,280 --> 00:06:53,880
Truth is, of all the videobooks
on the shelf,

120
00:06:53,960 --> 00:06:57,600
hers was the best. By far.

121
00:06:57,920 --> 00:07:00,880
The thing is, Paquita,
nowadays we use links.

122
00:07:01,240 --> 00:07:02,480
- What?
- Links.

123
00:07:02,560 --> 00:07:04,680
Links. And what is that?
Something from the computer, right?

124
00:07:04,760 --> 00:07:05,960
From the internet.

125
00:07:06,520 --> 00:07:07,880
Are we updated?

126
00:07:08,280 --> 00:07:09,680
PS Management...

127
00:07:10,720 --> 00:07:12,080
"PS Management..."

128
00:07:12,160 --> 00:07:14,320
..is looking for a triple threat actress.

129
00:07:14,680 --> 00:07:17,000
If that is you,
send your portfolio

130
00:07:17,200 --> 00:07:19,320
- to "info@..."
- "@..."

131
00:07:19,400 --> 00:07:21,880
PS Management.com. That’s it.

132
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:25,880
- No, it’s too long.
- What do you mean?

133
00:07:26,040 --> 00:07:28,560
This application allows to type

134
