A follower. Who’s following us?

137
00:07:38,280 --> 00:07:39,600
There’s nothing yet.

138
00:07:39,960 --> 00:07:41,720
It’ll change soon, right?
Let’s see.

139
00:07:42,960 --> 00:07:44,720
Don’t you put
dressing on that, Magüi?

140
00:07:44,800 --> 00:07:47,320
- I’m not a fan of vinegar.
- What about salt?

141
00:07:48,200 --> 00:07:50,080
- Salt is very bad.
- Really bad.

142
00:07:50,160 --> 00:07:52,800
- I quit salt, too.
- I see.

143
00:07:52,960 --> 00:07:55,320
- All right, have they answered?
- No.

144
00:07:55,480 --> 00:07:58,040
Magüi, we won’t find her this way.

145
00:08:04,400 --> 00:08:05,560
There are two seats over here.

146
00:08:05,800 --> 00:08:06,920
Hi!

147
00:08:07,520 --> 00:08:09,080
These stairs are wrong.

148
00:08:10,080 --> 00:08:12,440
Well, this is very modern...

149
00:08:12,880 --> 00:08:16,680
- Very contemporary.
- There are lots of people.

150
00:08:17,080 --> 00:08:18,600
Well, like we say in PS,

151
00:08:18,680 --> 00:08:21,560
an actress is created on stage,
that’s why we came

152
00:08:21,640 --> 00:08:23,920
to the theater performance
of "Primera fila" academy,

153
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:26,960
the best in Madrid.
We’ll see the work of these kids

154
00:08:27,040 --> 00:08:30,360
in a play written by Hedda Gabler.

155
00:08:30,520 --> 00:08:33,280
- Henrik Ibsen is who...
- All right, I see.

156
00:08:33,480 --> 00:08:36,360
The play was written by Henrik Ibsen

157
00:08:36,440 --> 00:08:38,200
and the adaptation was made

158
00:08:38,280 --> 00:08:41,400
by a girl named Hedda Gabler.
A student, surely.

159
00:08:43,440 --> 00:08:46,480
- God! I get it, I get it.
- It’s confusing, right?

160
00:08:46,560 --> 00:08:49,480
Yeah, the design...
Hedda Gabler is the name of the play,

161
00:08:49,560 --> 00:08:51,800
written by Henrik Ibsen.
It’s a well known work.

162
00:08:53,760 --> 00:08:54,920
It may be an action play.

163
00:08:56,680 --> 00:09:00,200
You must regard theater from afar.
If you’re a good actor...,

164
00:09:00,480 --> 00:09:02,480
- it is a foreground.
- Right.

165
00:09:02,840 --> 00:09:07,200
Look, there’s Canelón.
I’m going to talk to him.

166
00:09:07,360 --> 00:09:08,480
Fernando!

167
00:09:09,640 --> 00:09:12,440
Fernando.
Fernando Canelón, Fernando.

168
00:09:12,560 --> 00:09:13,520
Hi. Hello.

169
00:09:14,160 --> 00:09:15,040
How are you?

170
00:09:15,120 --> 00:09:16,600
- How are you?
- Very good.

171
00:09:16,680 --> 00:09:18,120
- Good?
- Let’s see the work

172
00:09:18,200 --> 00:09:20,200
- of these kids. I’m hunting.
- Hunting?

173
00:09:20,480 --> 00:09:22,600
With Magüi. Come here.
Magüi, this is Fernando.

174
00:09:22,680 --> 00:09:24,600
- He is the former you.
- Nice to meet you.

175
00:09:24,680 --> 00:09:26,360
“The former you”. Come on.

176
00:09:26,440 --> 00:09:28,760
- Always so witty.
- I’m mad at you. You never call.

177
00:09:28,840 --> 00:09:32,680
Yeah. Well, you know,
I’m busy 24/7. We really are.

178
00:09:32,760 --> 00:09:36,600
- At the office and everything.
- Come on, it’s not that bad!

179
00:09:36,680 --> 00:09:38,360
You’re doing great.
He’s doing great.

180
00:09:38,440 --> 00:09:41,560
When Fernando left the office,
he opened his own agency. Red Carpet.

181
00:09:41,640 --> 00:09:42,680
Yes.

182
00:09:42,760 --> 00:09:44,000
And now he even manages
Amaia Salamanca.

183
00:09:44,080 --> 00:09:45,760
- Well, Amaia?
- Yes.

184
00:09:45,840 --> 00:09:48,040
- I like her since the SMS series.
- She’s a working girl,

185
00:09:48,120 --> 00:09:50,000
- she’s very enthusiastic, right?
- Yeah.

186
00:09:50,080 --> 00:09:52,200
She wants to diversify her career,
get into singing.

187
00:09:52,280 --> 00:09:54,240
- Yeah, for you.
- Well, Fernandito.

188
00:09:59,960 --> 00:10:02,360
- That’s great.
- The play’s about to start.

189
00:10:02,440 --> 00:10:04,400
- Yeah, it’ll start soon.
- We’ll go to...

190
00:10:04,480 --> 00:10:06,280
- All right. We'll talk.
- We’ll talk later, Paquita.

191
00:10:06,360 --> 00:10:08,080
- Goodbye. Thanks.
- See you.

192
00:10:09,560 --> 00:10:12,320
He’s... very busy and we haven’t...

193
00:10:12,520 --> 00:10:15,520
- He seems to care for you.
- Yeah, yeah.

194
00:10:16,040 --> 00:10:18,560
Yeah, he’s a very nice man.
I love him a lot.

195
00:10:18,640 --> 00:10:19,800
I love him a lot.

196
00:10:21,200 --> 00:10:22,360
I’m nervous.

197
00:10:22,600 --> 00:10:25,400
Very. Imagine how they must feel.

198
00:10:26,120 --> 00:10:27,880
Whenever you’re ready.

199
00:10:35,200 --> 00:10:37,880
- What an old house.
- Yes.

200
00:10:38,640 --> 00:10:40,320
I don’t think they’ve woken up.

201
00:10:40,480 --> 00:10:43,360
You’re right, but let them rest.

202
00:10:48,720 --> 00:10:50,880
Perhaps, like all women,
you don’t feel...?

203
00:10:50,960 --> 00:10:53,240
Shut up already, I’m begging you.

204
00:10:56,760 --> 00:10:58,960
I’ve been thinking for quite a while
that my destiny

205
00:10:59,040 --> 00:11:02,160
is already traced.
Do you want to know it?

206
00:11:02,240 --> 00:11:04,520
- What do you think that is?
- See that girl?

207
00:11:04,600 --> 00:11:07,800
To be bored. Bored until I die.

208
00:11:26,680 --> 00:11:31,440
Live, live, die, die.
Live, live, die, die.

209
00:11:34,080 --> 00:11:36,160
Hedda must die!

210
00:11:41,560 --> 00:11:42,600
Bravo!

211
00:11:42,960 --> 00:11:44,000
Bravo!

212
00:11:45,200 --> 00:11:47,720
God, we’ve found her.
It’s her, it’s her.

213
00:11:47,800 --> 00:11:52,160
- She’s a triple threat.
- For sure. What a performance!

214
00:11:52,240 --> 00:11:53,160
I’ll stand up.

215
00:11:54,400 --> 00:11:55,560
She’s so classy.

216
00:11:55,640 --> 00:11:57,840
- Gorgeous!
- Bravo!

217
00:11:57,920 --> 00:11:58,920
Gorgeous!

218
00:12:00,760 --> 00:12:01,800
Bravo!

219
00:12:08,720 --> 00:12:12,040
Thank you very much.
Thank you.

220
00:12:12,960 --> 00:12:18,200
Specially to you, guys.
Congratulations. I’m very excited.

221
00:12:18,280 --> 00:12:22,680
I want a very important person
to join me on stage.

222
00:12:22,760 --> 00:12:28,240
He’s visiting us today and he would like
to say some words to these guys

223
00:12:28,320 --> 00:12:33,880
who today finish their remarkable path
at “Primera Fila” academy.

224
00:12:34,120 --> 00:12:37,480
Besides, he’s on the front row.
Come here, Fernando Canelón,

225
00:12:37,560 --> 00:12:40,760
from Red Carpet agency.
Welcome.

226
00:12:42,280 --> 00:12:45,520
Thank you very much.
Congratulations to all of you.

227
00:12:45,600 --> 00:12:49,360
You were amazing.
Here’s my card, just in case.

228
00:12:49,600 --> 00:12:51,320
All of you did really well,

229
00:12:51,400 --> 00:12:55,680
but you’re something else. Really.
Thanks a lot for the invitation

230
00:12:55,800 --> 00:12:58,640
to this performance.
It’s an honor to hear you

231
00:12:58,720 --> 00:13:00,600
and see your work
with these young people.

232
00:13:00,760 --> 00:13:04,240
Congratulations to all of you.
You’re in the right place

233
00:13:04,360 --> 00:13:07,720
because here you study the ideology,
the compromise and the harshness

234
00:13:07,800 --> 00:13:09,960
